Task 9: Create the keepalived configuration file.
Description Task 9: This task creates the keepalived.conf file in the /etc/keepalived directory, which contains the configuration for the keepalived service. The file has the correct owner, group, and permissions.

Task 10: Enable the keepalived service and ensure it is not masked.
Description Task 10: This task enables the keepalived service and ensures it is not masked, which allows the service to start automatically on boot.

Task 11: Flush the handlers to execute any pending tasks.
